# Docker build context ALLOW-LIST — a privacy control, not a speed tweak.
#
# This repository holds third-party material that must never enter an image:
# Sample_thesis_drafts/, the thesis text extracted under ml/dogfood/ and
# legacy/, and the course PDFs in Notes_On_Writing/ (CLAUDE.md, "Before this
# repository is ever made public"; ARCHITECTURE.md §9 "Repo hygiene").
#
# So everything is excluded, and only what an image needs is let back in.
# Adding a line here puts that path into every image built from the repo
# root: say why in the same change.

*

# services/engine/Dockerfile (the engine image)
!packages/core/requirements.txt
!packages/core/researchly/
!services/engine/requirements.txt
!services/engine/researchly_service/

# Re-excluded inside the allowed folders: bytecode and local clutter.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.DS_Store
